  "baseline_contract": "The primary baseline (host_fs) is a directory on the SAME bind-mounted host filesystem as the OrFS backing volume, so the two arms share the storage device and differ only in the filesystem stack. The tmpfs arm is an in-container RAM reference floor, reported for context only; it is not the headline comparator because RAM speed is not a filesystem property.",
  "caveat": "Single host, single run; wall-clock is host/load-sensitive. The container is CFS-capped and the host is under external load, so absolute times vary run to run; the same-device baseline and the order-balanced, repeated trials are what make the direction meaningful. The image-extraction workload is a SYNTHETIC OCI-layer-like tarball, not a real `docker pull`. No speedup is claimed without a measured external baseline in this same container.",
  "claim": "five real applications (git, sqlite3, tar, make/gcc, and an in-process metadata-heavy tree) driven end to end against a real OrFS FUSE mount and against external baselines on the same machine in the same container; the losses are published as losses",
